hadiths[97]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3100","Narrated by Hamad: A man has three sons, he said: One-third of my wealth is for the youngest son, the middle boy said: I have permission, and the eldest son said: I do not agree? Hammad said: The problem will be from the nine, of which the three (youngest boys) will be his share and the one who allowed it will be his share. And Hammad said: What remains will be returned equally to all, and Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: He who rejected (as if) rejected (his share) from himself."
"3101","Qazi Shareeh said: A man confessed to be (another's) brother, he said: He has to prove that he is his brother."
"3102","Harith Aqli said: A man at the time of his death confessed one thousand dirhams for mudarabat (trade), and one thousand for debt, and left only one thousand dirhams? He said: The debt will be paid first and if anything is left after that, it will be for Sahib Mudarabat (i.e. the one who gave dirhams for trade)."
"3103","On the authority of Shaabi, may God have mercy on him: A man died and left behind three hundred dirhams and three sons. After him, a man came and claimed one hundred dirhams on the deceased, and one of the three brothers also acknowledged it. Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: He will take his share from them."
"3104","It was narrated from Ash'at that Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said about a man who died and left his two sons and two thousand dirhams. Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him, said: The claimant will take what the present brother has and it will be said that you should find your brother and take half of what he has."
"3105","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: When some of the heirs acknowledge the debt (to the deceased), they will pay the debt from their share."
"3106","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: When two heirs who are true and testify to the debt, the debt will be paid from the total wealth."
"3107","Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman said: If an apostate (apostate) was killed, Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud considered his family as his heirs."
"3108","Abu Amr Shaybani said: Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (RA) declared the inheritance of the apostate to be his Muslim heirs."
"3109","It is narrated from the decree that Sayyiduna Ali (RA) decided to divide the inheritance of the murtad among his Muslim heirs."
"3110","The ruling said: A man who kills his brother intentionally will not be able to take anything from his inheritance, nor will anything be given to him from his dowry, and if the death of his brother is due to murder, then he will get a share of the inheritance, but will not get anything from the dowry. He said: Ata used to say the same."
"3111","Narrated by Khalas: Sayyiduna Ali (RA) narrated: A man hit his mother with a stone, so she died. He (the beater) asked his brothers for his share of the inheritance, so they said: You have no right to the inheritance. They came to Sayyiduna Ali (RA), so they made the death obligatory on the person who hit them and expelled them from the inheritance."
"3112","It is stated in the ruling that when a man kills his wife by murder, he will be expelled from the inheritance of Dit etc."
"3113","On the authority of Mujahid, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The murderer will not inherit anything from the deceased."
"3114","Mu'mar narrated on the authority of Qatadah that a man slandered his wife and brought witnesses (witnesses) as a result of which the woman was stoned, Qatadah said: He (the husband) will inherit her."
"3115","Abu Awana narrated to Hamad that a man was punished with lashes, Nu'man said: Perhaps as a result of which he died, Hamad said: They will inherit each other."
"3116","On the authority of Amir (Shaabi), may Allah have mercy on him, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A murderer will neither get an inheritance nor be a hajib (i.e. he will not deprive an heir)."
"3117","On the authority of Abu Amr Abdi, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A murderer will not be given an inheritance."
"3118","On the authority of Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) said: No one's murderer will be the inheritor of wrongdoing and intention."
"3119","On the authority of Taaws, may Allah have mercy on him, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A murderer will not inherit."
"3120","Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: When two lineages of the Magi gather together, the one who is the eldest will be the heir."
"3121","Hamad bin Abi Sulaiman said: In two genealogies, the one from whom the genealogy is correct will inherit, and the one from whom the genealogy is not correct will not inherit."
"3122","Imam Sha'bi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Ibn Mas'u (may Allah be pleased with them) said about the Magi that when they become Muslims, they will inherit from both their relatives."
"3123","Ibn Abi al-Zanad narrated from his father that Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may God have mercy on him) said about the wife of the prisoner that she would be his heir and the prisoner would be the heir of that woman."
"3124","Narrated by Ishaq bin Rashid. Umar bin Abdulaziz (may Allah have mercy on him) said about a captive who makes a will, he said: I consider his will as valid as long as he is on his religion unless he changes his religion."
"3125","Qazi Shareeh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: When a prisoner is in the possession of the enemy, he will be considered an heir."
"3126","Sufyan said who heard from Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, he narrated that Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, used to say: The captive will be considered as the heir."
"3127","Dawood (Ibn Abi Hind) said: Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, did not consider captives as heirs."
"3128","Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may God be pleased with him) wrote to Qazi Shareeh that he should not make the husband of a woman an heir without reason (binah), even if the woman brought him wrapped in a rag."
"3129","On the authority of Mansoor, Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: The Hamil (carried child) will be the heir."
"3130","On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Maryam: Dhamrah, Fazil bin Fazalah, Ibn Abi Awf, Rashid and Atiya all said: Hamil will not inherit."
"3131","Abdullah Ibn Aoun narrated: When Muhammad was mentioned about those who believed that Hamil was not the heir, he denied it and said: The Muhajirin and Ansar inherited each other according to the genealogy of Jahiliyyah."
"3132","It was narrated from Hisham that Hasan and Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: Hamil without a son will not be considered as an heir."
"3133","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Uthman (RA) did not consider Hamil as an heir."
"3134","Ash'ath bin Abi al-Sha'a'a said: A woman of Bani Muhareb confessed her relationship with her brother Jalib, so Abdullah bin Uqbah declared her (brother) the heir of her sister."
"3135","Narrated by Ibn Shihab, A person leaving the world should say, \I am the freedman of such and such a person.\"" He said: His wealth will be returned to the owners whom he had marked at the time of his departure from the world"," unless the heirs bring a strong argument other than that"," so in the light of evidence and evidence"," his inheritance will be given to Sahib Haqq."""
"3136","On the authority of Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud said: The son of Al-Zina is in the rank of Ibn Al-Mala'ina."
"3137","The ruling said: The person who claims to be the child of the son of Al-Zina will not be the heir of that child, nor will the son of Al-Zina be his heir."
"3138","It was narrated from Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ali Ibn Hussain (may Allah have mercy on him) did not consider the son of Al-Zina as an heir even if the man continued to claim him."
"3139","Sulaiman bin Yasar said: Whoever comes to a boy and thinks that he is his son, and he committed adultery with the boy's mother, and has no other claim to be the boy's father, then he will be the boy's heir. Bakir said: I asked ``Urwa about this, and he also answered like Sulaiman ibn Yasar, and ``Urwa said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The children belong to the bed-ridden (i.e. bed-ridden)"," and stones (i.e. stoning) are for the adulterer.\"""""
"3140","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: Ibn al-Ma'ina is like the son of Al-Zina, his mother will be his heir, and his mother's heirs are his heirs."
"3141","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Son of Al-Zina will not be made an heir."
"3142","Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said about the children of al-Zina that they will inherit from their mothers, and if a child is born and he dies, then (the other) will inherit his inheritance."
"3143","Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: The son of al-Zina (forbidden) will not be the heir, the heir will be the one whose father has not been issued a limit, or who is the owner of the child's mother due to marriage or purchase."
"3144","It was narrated from Ismail that Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: (If) a man commits adultery with a woman and then marries her, Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: There is nothing wrong with marrying her, except that she is pregnant (i.e. not married while pregnant), but the boy will not be attributed to her. (That is, the son of Al-Zina will neither be attributed to the father nor inherit)."
"3145","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed: \The boy who is reunited with his father after his death.\"" (That is"," after the deceased"," his heirs should claim that this is the child of our heir)"," then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decided that \""the boy is from the slave girl whose owner was her father at the time of intercourse"," so his lineage will be mixed with the one who mixed it. But the inheritance that is divided before it is mixed"," he will not have a share in the inheritance that has not been divided"," but he will have a share in it"," but the father with whom his lineage would have been mixed.\"" If he denied his parentage in his lifetime"," then he will not be accepted by the union of heirs (i.e."," his child will not be considered) and if the boy is from a slave girl whose owner was not his father or from a free woman with whom his father committed adultery"," then his parentage will never be proved from that man (even if the heirs of this man marry the child with him) and that child will not be the heir of that (adulterous) man"," even if his father committed adultery with him in his lifetime. claim that this is my child"," because he is the son of Al-Zina and he will join the people of his mother"," whether he is born from the womb of a free man or from the womb of a slave (after all"," the son of Al-Zina is"," and will not be an heir"," nor will he be included in the lineage)."""
"3146","Umayr bin Zayd said: I asked Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, about his slave who was born of adultery, and he replied: Do not sell him, do not eat his price, only you can take service from him."
"3147","Saeed said: Imam Zahri (may God have mercy on him) was asked about the son of Al-Zina who dies, he said: If it was from an Arab woman, his mother will inherit one-third and the rest of the property will be entered into the treasury, and even if he was the son of a slave who died, his mother will inherit one-third and what is left will be the heirs who freed her slave. Marwan said: I heard Imam Malik, may God have mercy on him, say this."
"3148","Amr ibn Shuaib narrated from his father, he narrated from his grandfather (Sayyidna Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided the total inheritance (wealth) of Ibn al-Mala’ina (a child whose father is a disbeliever) for the mother, because she was in trouble because of it."
"3149","On the authority of Zayd bin Wahhib, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to his maternal guardians about the son of Al-Zina: Take him, you will be his heirs, and you will also be responsible for his inheritance, and he will not be your heir."
"3150","Abu Amr al-Shaybani said: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) said: A freed slave should keep his wealth wherever he wants. Abdullah bin Zayd said: Shuba, may God have mercy on him, said: No one heard this from Salama bin Kaheel except me."
"3151","It is narrated from Yunus that Hasan, may God have mercy on him, was asked about the inheritance of a freed slave, and he replied: Every freed slave is a Saiba. (i.e. his inheritance is for the liberator)."
"3152","Abu Uthman said: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Both charity and saibah (freed slaves) are for their own day."
"3153","Zakariya said: Amir (al-Shaabi) may Allah have mercy on him was asked: If a Mamluk is freed as a Saiba, for whom is his walaa (right of inheritance)? Answered: He who has freed him (for him)."
"3154","Abd al-Rahman bin Amr said: During the time of Sayyidna Uthman, a slave died without an heir, Sayyidna Uthman ordered his property to be entered into the treasury."
"3155","Amir (Shaabi) reported on the authority of Masrooq, may God have mercy on him, that he said: If a man dies and there is no guardian, then his wealth should be spent in the manner that he had bequeathed, and if he had not bequeathed, then that wealth should be entered into Bait al-Mal."
"3156","On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Zamrah and Rashid bin Saad, etc., he said about a person who frees someone as a saiba, that the walaah of him (the freed one) is for the one who freed him, because he (the freer) has freed him from slavery, not freed him from the walaa (right of inheritance)."
"3157","Mansoor reported, Ibrahim and Sha'bi, may Allah have mercy on him, both said: There is no problem in selling Saibah's villa and Hiba."
"3158","Qasim said: A man freed a slave as Saibah and came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu and said: I had freed my slave as Saibah and this is his wealth (Tarqa)? Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud said: This is for you (i.e. your right). He said: I do not need it. He replied: Keep it, there are many heirs here."
"3159","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu said: When a (newborn) child makes a loud noise (i.e. cries) then it will inherit and prayers will be offered over it."
"3160","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: When a child cries, he will also inherit, and he will be made an heir, and his funeral prayer will also be offered."
"3161","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Every new-born child screams, and his scream is due to Satan squeezing his belly and he starts screaming, except for Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon him)."
"3162","Makhool said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A newborn will not inherit unless he utters a sound, even if he is born alive."
"3163","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: When the child makes a sound, the funeral prayer will be offered for him and he will be considered as an heir."
"3164","Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I consider sneezing as isthilal (the first sound of a child)."
"3165","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: A newborn will not be an heir unless he cries out, and the funeral prayer (funeral) will not be offered over him until he utters a voice, so when he utters a voice, the prayer will also be offered over him and he will be made an heir, and his death will also be perfect. That is, if someone kills him, the whole day will be as long as one man's day."
"3166","Yunus said: We asked Ibn Shihab Zuhri, may God have mercy on him, about a pregnancy that is aborted, and he said: The funeral prayer will not be offered over it, and the new-born prayer will not be offered until it cries."
"3167","Qatadah, may Allah have mercy on him, said: When two schools buy each other, one from its owner and the other from its owner, then (in such a case) the sale of the one who bought first will be valid (and the sale of the other will be nullified), and the people of Madinah say that the walaa (inheritance right) will go to the owner who sold it. Willa Ma Lak will be achieved."
"3168","It was narrated on the authority of Saeed, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, said: A free man who marries a slave woman has pledged his half, and a slave who marries a free woman has freed his half. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It means children."
"3169","On the authority of Shaibani (Sulaiman bin Firoz): Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: If a slave marries a woman and gives birth to a boy, if the woman is free, the maintenance (expenses) will be the responsibility of the mother (the slave is not the father's), and if the boy is also a slave, then his expenses will be borne by his masters."
"3170","Imam Amir Shaabi and Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: His rightful inheritance will belong to the one who first started freedom."
"3171","On the authority of Aban bin Taghlib, Haqm and Abu Na'im said: If a guarantor is made, the villa will be for him, and if a slave is made to work hard for freedom, then the inheritance will be divided between the owners."
"3172","It was narrated from Amir (may Allah have mercy on him) about a slave who is between two owners, one of the owners has freed him from his share, Sha'bi may Allah have mercy on him said: His freedom will be completed, if he does not have wealth, then labor will be made for the other half, and the one who frees will have the right of inheritance (walaa)."
"3173","Ibn Tawas narrated from his father: A slave is between two men (i.e. he is a slave of two) and one has freed him from his share and the other has withheld it. Tawas, may God have mercy on him, said: His inheritance will be divided between the two (owners)."
"3174","Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: His inheritance will be for the one who has withheld his share, and the whole of it is for the liberator, and the rest of its value will be (obligatory) on the liberator. This is what the people of Kufa say."
"3175","Narrated by Abdul Malik, narrated by Ata: A man who leaves behind only one school slave (whose money is fixed for his emancipation) and he has sons and daughters, will there be any portion of the slave's inheritance for the women? Ata said: For the women there will be a share of the money that still remains to be paid according to the Mukatba, and the walaa (inheritance right) will be only for the men and not for the women, except for the amount that they have fixed or freed."
"3176","On the authority of Layth, Taws, may God have mercy on him, said: The women of the Wala will not inherit except for the one whom they free (themselves) or the one whom they have freed."
"3177","On the authority of Mu'mar, Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: A man died and left a school slave, then that school also died. In this case, Ibn al-Masayb and Abu Salama bin Abd al-Rahman divided the money left from the school among the sons and daughters (male and female) of the owner. not me"
"3178","It was narrated from Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyidna Umar, Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Zayd (RA) said: Wala (the right of inheritance) belongs to the elders, and they did not consider women as inheritors of Wala, except for one whom they freed themselves or wrote a letter to free them for a fixed amount."
"3179","Abu Qalaba, Saeed bin Al-Masib, Sulayman bin Yasar said: Women will not inherit the Wala except for those women who have freed or studied."
"3180","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: Women will not inherit Wala except those women who freed him (the slave) or the slave whom they freed freed (someone) (and) except the accursed (cursing women), for she will inherit the one whom her son freed, the boy whose father refused (that this boy is not mine)."
"3181","It is narrated on the authority of Salem that his father Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA) used to inherit the freed slaves of Sayyidna Umar (RA) except the girls of Omar, that is, he did not give anything to the girls from the wives of the slaves."
"3182","Narrated by Khalid al-Huza: Abu Qalaba said: A woman died and left her children who inherited her property and also left slaves, then her sons also died. Abu Qalaba said: In such a case, the inheritance of the slaves will go to the woman's family. (i.e. brothers etc. whose share is not fixed in the duties of Shariat and they will be entitled to the rest of the share)."
"3183","Mansoor said: I asked Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him: A man corresponded with his slave and then died and left behind male and female heirs. He said: It will be the share of men only and not of women."
"3184","Yunus (Ibn Ubaid) narrated from Hasan, may God have mercy on him, that he used to say: If a woman dies and leaves a slave, the right of inheritance (wilaa) will belong to her sons, and if there are no sons, that is, if they die, the wilaa will return to the woman's family."
"3185","On the authority of Mughirah, Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: There is nothing for women among the slaves (the right of inheritance of a slave) except for a woman who frees a slave of her own accord."
"3186","Narrated by (Abdullah) Ibn Awun, Muhammad (Ibn Seerin may Allah have mercy on him) said: The freed slave of Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, died, so Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, asked Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, is there anything from the inheritance for the daughters of Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him? So he replied: In my opinion there is nothing for them, if you want to give then you can give them something."
"3187","It was narrated from Hisham that his father said: The rightful owner of the villa will be the one who is entitled to the inheritance."
"3188","It was narrated from Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm that a woman from Bani Muhareb bequeathed the inheritance of her slave to him and freed him. The slave gave his inheritance to Abd al-Rahman bin Amr bin Hazm, and then the woman died, and the owner of that slave filed a case with Sayyiduna Uthman. Make whoever you want as your guardian, so he made Abd al-Rahman bin Amr bin Hazm his guardian. That is, made the heir of the villa."
"3189","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale and giving away of wealth."
"3190","It is also narrated from this chain of narrators on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) in the same way as it has been translated above."
"3191","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, used to say: Vala cannot be sold or given away, and vala is for the one who freed (the slave)."
"3192","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Wala is a relationship like the relationship of lineage, it cannot be sold or given away."
"3193","Qatadah (bin Duamah) said: Hasan and Saeed bin Al-Musayyib, may God have mercy on him, have disliked (i.e. regarded as makruh) the sale of Wala."
"3194","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Will not be sold, will a man's neck be eaten twice?"
"3195","It is narrated from Ata that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) said: There are six duties, we do not believe in these (issues)."
"3196","Ayyub bin al-Harith said: The case of two girls, mother, father and husband came to Qazi Shareeh, so he decided it (i.e. without Awl, so his share was reduced). Therefore, when the husband complained about it in the mosque, Abdullah bin Rabah sent for Qazi Shareeh and asked Qazi Shareeh: What do you say about this? He replied: This man considers me cruel and I consider him a fajr because he has given the fatwa and the entire decision has been hidden. This man said: Then what do you say about the two girls, parents and husband? He said: For the husband there is a quarter of the entire property, and for both the mother and the father there is two hundredths (sixths) (i.e. six and six), the rest is for the girls. Abdullah bin Rabah said: I have not criticized you, Allah has explained your shortcomings. Two-thirds (four) for both girls, Sadsan (1.1) for parents and one-fourth for husband, and this problem will be from seven and a half, and in this problem, Awl will have to work."
